From: Kaonic <dev@beechat.network>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: stm32mp1: keep pll3_q and pll4_q running for the SCMI-owned SPI6

SPI6 sits in the secure domain: Linux enables its kernel clock through
SCMI (CK_SCMI_SPI6) and never sees the parent that OP-TEE selected for it.
When that parent is a PLL output, nothing in Linux holds it, so the late
clk_disable_unused pass gates it and SPI6 is left with no clock at all. The
first register access to the controller then hangs the bus - reproduced as a
kernel livelock on insmod of the RF215 driver, independent of the SPI rate,
on pll3_q and pll4_q alike.

HSI works only because it is always on, and it limits SPI6 to 16 MHz. Mark
both PLL Q outputs critical, the way pll2_r already is, so a PLL-sourced
SPI6 keeps its clock and can run at 25 MHz whichever of the two OP-TEE
picks (pll3_q = 100 MHz is the one in use).

---
 drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp1.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp1.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/stm32/clk-stm32mp1.c
@@ -1932,7 +1932,7 @@ static const struct clock_config stm32mp1_clock_cfg[] = {
 		  _NO_MUX,
 		  _DIV(RCC_PLL3CFGR2, 0, 7, 0, NULL)),
 
-	COMPOSITE(PLL3_Q, "pll3_q", PARENT("pll3"), 0,
+	COMPOSITE(PLL3_Q, "pll3_q", PARENT("pll3"), CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		  _GATE(RCC_PLL3CR, 5, 0),
 		  _NO_MUX,
 		  _DIV_DUTY_CYCLE(RCC_PLL3CFGR2, 8, 7, 0, NULL)),
@@ -1947,7 +1947,7 @@ static const struct clock_config stm32mp1_clock_cfg[] = {
 		  _NO_MUX,
 		  _DIV(RCC_PLL4CFGR2, 0, 7, 0, NULL)),
 
-	COMPOSITE(PLL4_Q, "pll4_q", PARENT("pll4"), 0,
+	COMPOSITE(PLL4_Q, "pll4_q", PARENT("pll4"), CLK_IS_CRITICAL,
 		  _GATE(RCC_PLL4CR, 5, 0),
 		  _NO_MUX,
 		  _DIV(RCC_PLL4CFGR2, 8, 7, 0, NULL)),
